IMPORT prelude

-- Developmental Investment Fund Act 2000 (Singapore) -- what counts as a "developmental purpose" and a "financial year" (s 2), what
-- goes into the Fund and how its net investment income is reckoned (s 3), what the moneys may be withdrawn and applied for and where
-- the Financial Procedure Act 1966 s 7(3) is disapplied (s 4), who controls the Fund and its accounts (ss 5, 6(1)), the managing
-- Minister's revenue duty (s 6(2)(a)), surplus transfers (s 8), the conditions on any withdrawal or payment (s 9), who may be an
-- accounting officer and what that officer is deemed to be (s 17(3), (4)), and which statements go to the Auditor-General (s 18).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/DIFA2000.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; it is an informal
-- consolidation "version in force from 31/1/2022". The latest amending Act annotated in the text and listed in the Legislative History
-- is Act 35 of 2021 (Government Borrowing (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2021, in force 31 January 2022), which repealed Part 3
-- (ss 10 to 16) and deleted ss 3(1)(b), 7(2) and 20(b). The source metadata records the version as current at 1 October 2026.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0167 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. The answer is: very little. The Act is a Government fund statute (ss 1-9, 17-20 survive). It gives no person a right,
-- creates no offence and no penalty, and has no application procedure. A business meets it only as a possible investee -- the Fund
-- may buy its securities, help form a company or invest in property for a developmental purpose -- and a public-authority officer
-- meets it on appointment as an accounting officer. The scope is therefore nearly the whole surviving Act.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 1; the definitions of "invest", "property", "securities" beyond their use in the enumerations below; s 3(2) (the
-- Fund is a Government fund of public moneys) except as a comment; s 6(1) orders themselves and s 6(2)(b), (c) (prudent-investor
-- and developmental-objective duties: not decidable on facts); s 7(1) except as the "charged upon the Fund" flag; s 17(1), (2); s 19
-- except as the reason the Financial Procedure Act applies by default; s 20 (no regulations were retrieved). What s 7(3) of the
-- Financial Procedure Act 1966 and s 20 of that Act say was NOT read: that Act is not in this deposit.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Developmental Investment Fund Act 2000 -- the Fund`

§§ `2 -- developmental purpose`

-- s 2: "developmental purpose" means (a) to promote, assist in or facilitate the establishment, development or expansion of any
-- industry or class of business enterprise "that will enhance, directly or indirectly, economic growth and employment opportunities
-- in Singapore, that enjoys good export market prospects or that will enhance Singapore's international competitiveness"; (b) to
-- construct, improve, extend or replace buildings, works, plant, machinery, equipment "or other infrastructure required in respect of
-- or connected with the economic development or general welfare of Singapore"; (c) "to reclaim or develop any land IN SINGAPORE or to
-- commercially exploit or apply any scientific knowledge or technology"; or (d) research, survey, investigation or other work
-- "preparatory to" (a), (b) or (c).
--
-- Land must be in Singapore; technology carries no place limit in (c). (a) is met by any ONE of its three tests.
DECLARE Aim IS ONE OF
    `expanding an industry that will create jobs in Singapore`
    `expanding a business with good export market prospects`
    `building a power plant for Singapore`
    `building a hospital for the general welfare of Singapore`
    `reclaiming land in Singapore`
    `reclaiming land abroad`
    `commercialising a new technology`
    `a feasibility survey for a land reclamation in Singapore`
    `a feasibility survey for a land reclamation abroad`
    `supporting the general budget`
    `earning a financial return only`

GIVEN `the aim` IS AN Aim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the aim is a developmental purpose` IF
    CONSIDER `the aim`
    WHEN `expanding an industry that will create jobs in Singapore` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `expanding a business with good export market prospects` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `building a power plant for Singapore` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `building a hospital for the general welfare of Singapore` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `reclaiming land in Singapore` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `commercialising a new technology` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a feasibility survey for a land reclamation in Singapore` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 2: "financial year", in relation to the Fund, "means a period of 12 months ending on 31 March in any year". The year returned is
-- the calendar year in which that 31 March falls.
GIVEN `month` IS A NUMBER, `calendar year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the financial year ends on 31 March of` MEANS
    IF `month` AT MOST 3 THEN `calendar year` ELSE `calendar year` PLUS 1

§§ `3 -- what goes in, and net investment income`

-- s 3(1): into the Fund "must be paid" (a) moneys appropriated from the Consolidated Fund and authorised to be paid in; (c) other
-- revenues of Singapore allocated to it by written law; and (d) "the net income from investments" ((b) deleted by Act 35 of 2021).
-- (2): the Fund "must be regarded as a Government fund and as comprising public moneys".
-- (3): net income is "the amount ascertained by adding to, or deducting from, the income received from investments ... any profit
-- derived or loss sustained (as the case may be) from the realisation of those investments".
GIVEN `income received` IS A NUMBER, `realised profit` IS A NUMBER, `realised loss` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the net income from investments` MEANS
    `income received` PLUS `realised profit` MINUS `realised loss`

§§ `4 -- what the moneys may be applied for`

-- s 4(1): the moneys "may be withdrawn and applied for all or any of the following purposes ONLY": (a) to invest in, subscribe for or
-- acquire securities in any public authority, corporation or body corporate for any developmental purpose; (b) to form or participate
-- in forming a company for any developmental purpose; (c) to invest in any funds or property "(whether within or outside Singapore)"
-- for any developmental purpose; (d) charges, fees or expenses incidental to (a), (b) and (c); (e) expenses mentioned in s 7.
-- There is no head for a grant, a subsidy or a running cost of Government.
DECLARE Use IS ONE OF
    `subscribing for shares in a company`
    `buying bonds issued by a statutory board`
    `forming a company`
    `investing in an overseas fund`
    `buying property`
    `paying brokerage on an investment`
    `paying the Fund's administration expenses`
    `making an outright grant to a business`
    `paying a ministry's running costs`

GIVEN `the use` IS A Use
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use is an investment head` IF
    CONSIDER `the use`
    WHEN `subscribing for shares in a company` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `buying bonds issued by a statutory board` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `forming a company` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `investing in an overseas fund` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `buying property` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- For (d), `the aim` is the aim of the investment the charge is incidental to. For (e), the aim is irrelevant.
GIVEN `the use` IS A Use, `the aim` IS AN Aim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the moneys may be applied` IF
        (`the use is an investment head` `the use` AND `the aim is a developmental purpose` `the aim`)
    OR  (`the use` EQUALS `paying brokerage on an investment` AND `the aim is a developmental purpose` `the aim`)
    OR  `the use` EQUALS `paying the Fund's administration expenses`

-- s 4(2): "Section 7(3) of the Financial Procedure Act 1966 does not apply to the application of any moneys in the Fund in accordance
-- with subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c)." s 19: otherwise the Financial Procedure Act 1966 and its regulations apply to the Fund.
GIVEN `the use` IS A Use
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 7(3) of the Financial Procedure Act applies` IF
    NOT `the use is an investment head` `the use`

§§ `5, 6(1) and 9 -- who controls, and who may authorise a payment`

-- s 5(1): the Minister (for finance) is responsible for all moneys "not assigned to any responsible Minister under section 6(1)".
-- (2): despite any assignment, the Minister "remains overall responsible". s 6(1): by order, an account within the Fund may be placed
-- under a "responsible Minister".
-- s 9(1): moneys must not be withdrawn "unless they are charged upon the Fund or are authorised or directed to be withdrawn or
-- transferred under this Act". (2): no payment "unless the payment is authorised by the Minister or, in the case of moneys in an
-- account established under section 6(1), unless the payment is authorised by the responsible Minister in charge of that account".
--
-- Read literally, for account moneys only the responsible Minister may authorise the payment; the Minister's overall responsibility
-- under s 5(2) is not listed as an alternative in s 9(2).
DECLARE Authoriser IS ONE OF
    `the Minister for Finance`
    `the responsible Minister for the account`
    `another Minister`
    `a senior civil servant`

GIVEN `in an assigned account` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Authoriser
`who has day-to-day control` MEANS
    IF `in an assigned account` THEN `the responsible Minister for the account` ELSE `the Minister for Finance`

GIVEN `in an assigned account` IS A BOOLEAN, `the authoriser` IS AN Authoriser
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payment is properly authorised` IF
    IF `in an assigned account`
    THEN `the authoriser` EQUALS `the responsible Minister for the account`
    ELSE `the authoriser` EQUALS `the Minister for Finance`

GIVEN `charged upon the Fund` IS A BOOLEAN, `authorised or directed under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the withdrawal is permitted by section 9(1)` IF
    `charged upon the Fund` OR `authorised or directed under this Act`

§§ `6(2)(a) -- the revenue duty`

-- s 6(2)(a): the duty "to manage the Fund or account ... so that the revenue of the Fund or account is not less than sufficient to
-- meet expenses which are properly chargeable to the Fund or account".
GIVEN `revenue` IS A NUMBER, `chargeable expenses` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the revenue duty is met` IF
    `revenue` AT LEAST `chargeable expenses`

§§ `8 -- surplus transfers`

-- s 8(1): the Minister may "by warrant under his or her hand" transfer to the Consolidated Fund moneys "not immediately required".
-- (2): the Minister may, "after consulting the relevant responsible Minister", by warrant transfer to the Fund moneys from an account.
GIVEN `by warrant of the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Minister thinks them not immediately required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a transfer to the Consolidated Fund is authorised` IF
    `by warrant of the Minister` AND `the Minister thinks them not immediately required`

GIVEN `by warrant of the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN, `after consulting the responsible Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a transfer from an account back to the Fund is authorised` IF
    `by warrant of the Minister` AND `after consulting the responsible Minister`

§§ `17(3), (4) -- accounting officers`

-- s 17(3): every responsible Minister "must appoint a public officer or an officer of any public authority to be an accounting
-- officer" for the account. s 2: "public authority" means "any board or authority established by or under any written law to perform
-- or discharge any public function".
-- (4): an officer of a public authority so appointed "is deemed to be" (a) a public officer for the purposes of the Financial
-- Procedure Act 1966, and s 20 of that Act applies "even though the officer is not or was not in the employment of the Government";
-- and (b) "a public servant for the purposes of the Penal Code 1871".
-- Whether a public officer is already a public servant under the Penal Code is not decided here (that Code is not in this deposit).
DECLARE Candidate IS ONE OF
    `a public officer`
    `an officer of a statutory board`
    `an employee of a private fund manager`
    `an accountant in private practice`

GIVEN `the candidate` IS A Candidate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the candidate may be appointed accounting officer` IF
    CONSIDER `the candidate`
    WHEN `a public officer` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an officer of a statutory board` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the candidate` IS A Candidate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appointee is deemed a public servant by section 17(4)` IF
    `the candidate` EQUALS `an officer of a statutory board`

§§ `18 -- what goes to the Auditor-General`

-- s 18: as soon as practicable after each financial year the Minister must submit to the Auditor-General (a) the financial statements
-- for the Fund, or (b) "if accounts have been established under section 6(1), the consolidated financial statements", and the
-- Auditor-General "must then audit and report on them".
DECLARE Statements IS ONE OF
    `the financial statements for the Fund`
    `the consolidated financial statements for the Fund`

GIVEN `accounts have been established` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Statements
`the statements submitted for audit` MEANS
    IF `accounts have been established` THEN `the consolidated financial statements for the Fund` ELSE `the financial statements for the Fund`
